// `~x` (the keyword `unquote`) marks an argument of a deep splice
// (`f!!(~a, b)`, readable `splice f(~a, b)`) to be evaluated at compile
// time. Deep splices build an `ast` carrier that does not exist yet, so the
// splice stops at the `vm.call_quote` seam instead of running as a plain
// call (docs/keyword_roadmap.md K4). The plain call before it runs: 1 + 2 = 3.
fn add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 => a + b;

fn main() {
    let a = 1;
    print(add(a, 2));
    print(add!!(~a, 2));
}
